{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"generated":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"},"abstract":[{"text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", collected by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","type":"heading","text":"1. Give the library a macro","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6576_6E74"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the set for its users:"}]},{"code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSets.LinkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"imports LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “cannot find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘LinkerSets’ in scope” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvents.all"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set is read in one place."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}]},{"anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","type":"heading","text":"2. Read the set beside the list","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:"}]},{"code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}]},{"anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","type":"heading","text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","level":3},{"code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type, is refused with a message, as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},{"text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","type":"heading","text":"4. Delete the list","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}]},{"code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}]},{"anchor":"Other-registries","type":"heading","text":"Other registries","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Routes"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")"},{"type":"text","text":", read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Route>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Migrations"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", read as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", sorted by a version the migration declares.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dependency registrations"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)"},{"type":"text","text":", each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stable but not one you choose (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","role":"article","title":"Finding records","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","abstract":[{"text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"title":"LinkerSets","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Declaring a kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetKind":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetKind","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetkind","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LinkerSetKind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"title":"What the macros refuse","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSet":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkerset","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSet","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"LinkerSet","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}]}}}